---
import ContentLayout from '../layouts/ContentLayout.astro';
import ProductInterfacePreview from '../components/ProductInterfacePreview.astro';
import { softwareProducts } from '../data/softwareProducts';
---

<ContentLayout
  title="Software & Apps | Fluxology, Inc."
  description="Explore software products developed and published by Fluxology, Inc., including active iOS development and supporting decision, research and comparison tools."
  eyebrow="Software publishing"
  heading="Independent software products from Fluxology, Inc."
  intro="Fluxology, Inc. develops and publishes its own applications and digital tools. Software is a current corporate activity: products are built for end users, not as contract app-development services for clients."
>
  <section class="portfolio-intro" aria-labelledby="portfolio-status-heading">
    <h2 id="portfolio-status-heading">Current software activity</h2>
    <p>
      Software development is active during Fluxology's current foundation period. The company is building iOS
      applications for future App Store distribution while also operating web-based research, comparison and
      workflow tools used in ongoing product development. Product scope, support material and privacy disclosures
      are finalized before each public release.
    </p>

    <div class="portfolio-status-grid" role="list" aria-label="Software portfolio status">
      <div class="portfolio-status-card" role="listitem">
        <strong>{softwareProducts.length}</strong>
        <span>named products in active development</span>
      </div>
      <div class="portfolio-status-card" role="listitem">
        <strong>iOS</strong>
        <span>applications in active development</span>
      </div>
      <div class="portfolio-status-card" role="listitem">
        <strong>Web</strong>
        <span>supporting dashboards in active use</span>
      </div>
      <div class="portfolio-status-card" role="listitem">
        <strong>Fluxology, Inc.</strong>
        <span>developer and publisher</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="product-portfolio" aria-labelledby="products-heading">
    <div class="section-lead">
      <p class="apps-eyebrow">Product portfolio</p>
      <h2 id="products-heading">Products built around decisions, not generic dashboards.</h2>
      <p>
        Both current products organize messy external information into explicit states: what is known, what is
        unresolved, what changed, and what action comes next. The interfaces below are representative visualizations
        of those workflows rather than live user data.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="product-stack">
      {softwareProducts.map((product, index) => (
        <article id={product.id} class:list={['app-product', { reversed: index % 2 === 1 }]} aria-labelledby={`${product.id}-heading`}>
          <div class="app-product-copy">
            <div class="app-product-heading">
              <img src={product.icon} alt="" width="56" height="56" aria-hidden="true" loading="lazy" />
              <div>
                <p class="app-status"><span aria-hidden="true"></span>{product.status}</p>
                <h3 id={`${product.id}-heading`}>{product.name}</h3>
                <p class="app-category">{product.category}</p>
              </div>
            </div>

            <p class="app-summary">{product.shortDescription}</p>
            <p class="app-detail">{product.longDescription}</p>

            <div class="app-detail-columns">
              <div>
                <h4>Core capabilities</h4>
                <ul>
                  {product.capabilities.map((capability) => <li>{capability}</li>)}
                </ul>
              </div>
              <div>
                <h4>Workflow states</h4>
                <div class="workflow-pills" role="list">
                  {product.workflow.map((state) => <span role="listitem">{state}</span>)}
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <ProductInterfacePreview
            productName={product.name}
            labels={product.previewLabels}
            mirrored={index % 2 === 1}
          />
        </article>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="development-model">
    <h2>How Fluxology develops software</h2>
    <div class="content-card-grid">
      <article class="content-card">
        <h3>Problem-specific products</h3>
        <p>
          Products start from a concrete workflow that needs better structure: comparing offices using complete
          occupancy cost, or comparing purchases when shipping and currency materially change the apparent deal.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="content-card">
        <h3>Explicit uncertainty</h3>
        <p>
          Unknown information stays unknown. Office Scout distinguishes verified costs from costs needing
          verification; Fluxology Deals distinguishes resolved destination shipping from unresolved estimates.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="content-card">
        <h3>Persistent history</h3>
        <p>
          Useful prior states are preserved rather than silently disappearing. Product workflows retain listing
          changes, status history or prior decisions when that history remains useful to the user.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="content-card">
        <h3>User-owned workflow state</h3>
        <p>
          The supporting dashboards keep personal review states and notes in the user's browser rather than making
          those personal workflow fields part of the shared server listing feed.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Publishing, support and release status</h2>
    <p>
      Apps and related intellectual property are developed and published by Fluxology, Inc. The corporation is the
      legal entity responsible for product distribution, customer support and applicable product policies. The
      proposed trade, fabrication and homestead operating names described elsewhere on this site are future
      operating lines of the same corporation; they are not software publishers.
    </p>
    <p>
      The applications described here remain in development and are not represented as currently available on the
      App Store. When an individual app is released, Fluxology will publish that app's dedicated support and privacy
      pages under its own <code>/apps/&lt;app-name&gt;/</code> path together with applicable store links.
    </p>

    <div class="content-callout app-contact-block">
      <div>
        <span>Product support</span>
        <a href="/support/">fluxology.ca/support/</a>
      </div>
      <div>
        <span>Corporate privacy</span>
        <a href="/privacy/">fluxology.ca/privacy/</a>
      </div>
      <div>
        <span>General contact</span>
        <a href="mailto:info@fluxology.ca">info@fluxology.ca</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</ContentLayout>

<style>
  .portfolio-status-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(4, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: var(--spacing-md);
    margin-top: var(--spacing-xl);
  }

  .portfolio-status-card {
    display: flex;
    min-height: 132px;
    padding: var(--spacing-lg);
    border: 1px solid rgba(168, 218, 220, 0.18);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    background: rgba(9, 30, 45, 0.62);
    flex-direction: column;
    justify-content: center;
  }

  .portfolio-status-card strong {
    color: #fff;
    font-family: var(--font-corporate-heading);
    font-size: clamp(1.35rem, 2.5vw, 1.9rem);
  }

  .portfolio-status-card span {
    margin-top: 0.35rem;
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.55);
    font-size: var(--font-size-sm);
    line-height: 1.45;
  }

  .section-lead {
    max-width: 760px;
  }

  .apps-eyebrow {
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-sm);
    color: var(--corporate-accent-silver);
    font-size: var(--font-size-xs);
    font-weight: var(--font-weight-bold);
    letter-spacing: var(--letter-spacing-wider);
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .product-stack {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--spacing-2xl);
    margin-top: var(--spacing-2xl);
  }

  .app-product {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 0.96fr) minmax(360px, 1.04fr);
    gap: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 4rem);
    align-items: center;
    scroll-margin-top: 7rem;
    padding: clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 2.75rem);
    border: 1px solid rgba(168, 218, 220, 0.2);
    border-radius: var(--radius-xl);
    background:
      radial-gradient(circle at 100% 0%, rgba(58, 134, 255, 0.08), transparent 23rem),
      rgba(9, 30, 45, 0.72);
  }

  .app-product.reversed .app-product-copy {
    order: 2;
  }

  .app-product.reversed :global(.product-interface-preview) {
    order: 1;
  }

  .app-product-heading {
    display: flex;
    gap: var(--spacing-md);
    align-items: center;
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-lg);
  }

  .app-product-heading img {
    width: 56px;
    height: 56px;
    padding: 9px;
    border: 1px solid rgba(168, 218, 220, 0.22);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.05);
  }

  .app-status {
    display: flex;
    gap: 0.45rem;
    align-items: center;
    margin: 0 0 0.15rem;
    color: #a8dadc;
    font-size: var(--font-size-xs);
    font-weight: var(--font-weight-semibold);
    letter-spacing: var(--letter-spacing-wide);
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .app-status span {
    width: 7px;
    height: 7px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: #63d8a0;
    box-shadow: 0 0 0 4px rgba(99, 216, 160, 0.1);
  }

  .app-product h3 {
    margin: 0;
    color: #fff;
    font-family: var(--font-corporate-heading);
    font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 3vw, 2.5rem);
  }

  .app-category {
    margin: 0.15rem 0 0;
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.5);
    font-size: var(--font-size-sm);
  }

  .app-summary {
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.88);
    font-size: var(--font-size-lg);
    line-height: 1.65;
  }

  .app-detail {
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.68);
  }

  .app-detail-columns {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.35fr) minmax(0, 0.65fr);
    gap: var(--spacing-lg);
    margin-top: var(--spacing-xl);
  }

  .app-detail-columns h4 {
    margin: 0 0 var(--spacing-sm);
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.9);
    font-family: var(--font-corporate-heading);
    font-size: var(--font-size-md);
  }

  .app-detail-columns ul {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .workflow-pills {
    display: flex;
    gap: 0.45rem;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }

  .workflow-pills span {
    padding: 0.35rem 0.65rem;
    border: 1px solid rgba(58, 134, 255, 0.22);
    border-radius: var(--radius-full);
    background: rgba(58, 134, 255, 0.08);
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.68);
    font-size: var(--font-size-xs);
  }

  .development-model .content-card-grid {
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
  }

  .app-contact-block {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: var(--spacing-lg);
  }

  .app-contact-block div {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.3rem;
  }

  .app-contact-block span {
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.5);
    font-size: var(--font-size-xs);
    font-weight: var(--font-weight-semibold);
    letter-spacing: var(--letter-spacing-wide);
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  code {
    padding: 0.12em 0.35em;
    border: 1px solid rgba(168, 218, 220, 0.14);
    border-radius: 0.3rem;
    background: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.18);
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.82);
  }

  @media (max-width: 920px) {
    .portfolio-status-grid {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    }

    .app-product {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .app-product.reversed .app-product-copy,
    .app-product.reversed :global(.product-interface-preview) {
      order: initial;
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 680px) {
    .portfolio-status-grid,
    .development-model .content-card-grid,
    .app-contact-block,
    .app-detail-columns {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .app-product {
      padding: var(--spacing-lg);
    }
  }
</style>
